## Test Smell Audit — Academic 19-Smell Catalog (testsmells.org)

**Target:** `DataAccess.IntegrationTests/UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs`
**Framework:** MSTest 4.1 (.NET 10)
**Integration calibration:** Applied — class has `[TestCategory("Integration")]`

---

### Summary Dashboard

| Severity | Smell Count | Affected Tests |
|----------|-------------|----------------|
| High     | 3           | 3              |
| Medium   | 1           | 1              |
| Low      | 0           | 0              |
| **Total**| **4**       | **4**          |

---

### Findings by Severity

#### ❶ Sleepy Test — HIGH

**Method:** `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` (line 87)

```csharp
Thread.Sleep(3000); // ← blocks 3 seconds, non-deterministic
```

**Why it's still High even for integration tests:** Sleep-based synchronisation is flaky regardless of test scope. The delay may be too short on CI or wastefully long locally.

**Fix:**
```csharp
// Poll with timeout instead of fixed sleep
var cts = new CancellationTokenSource(TimeSpan.FromSeconds(5));
while (!_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id))
{
    await Task.Delay(50, cts.Token);
}
Assert.IsTrue(_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id));
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Flaky CI failures; artificially slow test suite.

---

#### ❷ Conditional Test Logic — HIGH

**Method:** `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` (lines 101–108)

```csharp
if (loaded is PremiumUser premium)
{
    Assert.IsTrue(premium.DiscountRate > 0);
}
else
{
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);
}
```

**Why High:** One branch is never exercised deterministically — the test silently passes regardless of the actual type, hiding a gap.

**Fix:** Split into two explicit tests:
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_WhenStandard_ReturnsCorrectName() { /* assert standard path */ }

[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_WhenPremium_HasPositiveDiscount() { /* seed a PremiumUser, assert discount */ }
```

**Risk if unfixed:** A regression in one type path goes undetected forever.

---

#### ❸ Assertion-Free Test (Unknown Test) — HIGH

**Method:** `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors` (lines 113–119)

```csharp
for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
{
    _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
}
// ← no assertion; passes even if inserts silently fail
```

**Fix:**
```csharp
for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));

var users = _repository.ListAll();
Assert.AreEqual(100, users.Count);
```

**Risk if unfixed:** False confidence — test always passes, verifies nothing.

---

#### ❹ Assertion Roulette — MEDIUM

**Method:** `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` (lines 35–38)

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name);
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email);
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0);
// ← 4 assertions, none with a failure message
```

**Why Medium:** When one fails in CI, the failure output says `Assert.AreEqual failed. Expected:<Alice>. Actual:<null>` with no context about *which property* was wrong without reading source.

**Fix:** Add message parameters:
```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded, "User should be retrievable after insert");
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name, "Name should persist");
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email, "Email should persist");
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0, "Auto-generated ID should be positive");
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Slower failure diagnosis in CI logs.

---

### Smell-Free Patterns ✓

| Test | Notes |
|------|-------|
| `UpdateUser_ModifiesExistingRecord` | Clear arrange-act-assert, focused assertions |
| `DeleteUser_RemovesFromDatabase` | Single assertion verifying the key behavior |
| `ListUsers_ReturnsAllInserted` | Count `3` is self-documenting (3 items just added) — not a Magic Number smell |
| `InsertUser_ConcurrentInserts_MaintainsIntegrity` | Proper async/await, focused assertion |

The in-memory SQLite approach avoids **Mystery Guest** entirely — no external resources. **General Fixture** is clean: both `_connection` and `_repository` are used by every test.

---

### Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Effort | Action |
|----------|-------|--------|--------|
| 1 | Assertion-Free Test | ~2 min | Add count assertion to `BulkInsert` |
| 2 | Conditional Test Logic | ~5 min | Split `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` into two tests |
| 3 | Sleepy Test | ~10 min | Replace `Thread.Sleep` with poll-and-timeout |
| 4 | Assertion Roulette | ~3 min | Add message strings to `InsertUser` assertions |

Items 1–3 prevent **silent false-passes** or **flaky failures** — fix them first. Item 4 is a maintainability improvement.
